  "notes": [
    {
      "row": "notes",
      "title": "Flow matching, not DDPM",
      "text": "The model predicts a velocity, not an epsilon. The scheduler (FlowUniPC or FlowDPM) integrates it from t = 1 to t = 0. That is why there is no alpha/beta schedule anywhere in the model code.",
      "code": [
        {
          "role": "call_site",
          "src": "wan.t2v",
          "lines": [
            314,
            321
          ],
          "expect": {
            "symbol": "WanT2V.generate",
            "first": "sample_scheduler = FlowUniPCMultistepScheduler(",
            "sha": "0c4d8753",
            "span": [
              208,
              383
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "row": "notes",
      "title": "What is frozen at training time",
      "text": "umT5 and the VAE are frozen and are not even loaded during a LoRA finetune of the DiT — their outputs are cached to disk. Only WanModel's 30 blocks, the two embedders and the head carry gradients.",
